// Outfit, as TTF bytes the OG card can actually draw with.
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS A BLOB, when public/outfit.woff2 already exists:
//
//   - Satori (next/og) ships no system fonts. A glyph it has not been handed
//     is not drawn at all — no fallback, just a gap — so the card's typeface
//     is not a preference here, it is the difference between text and holes.
//   - It cannot read woff2. TTF, OTF or WOFF only.
//   - public/outfit.woff2 is ASCII (96 codepoints). No u-umlaut, no middot.
//     'Rudesheim' and '8 days · 4 stays' would both come out broken.
//   - The route runs on the edge runtime, which has no filesystem — and
//     fetching public/ over HTTP is the exact shape that already cost this
//     repo a bad deploy (see the template() fallback in pages/t/[s].js:
//     public/ is CDN, not lambda disk). Inlined bytes cannot 404.
//
// Two static weights rather than the variable font: Satori's variable-font
// support is shaky, and the card only ever uses these two.
//
// Subset to Latin-1 + Latin Extended-A + the punctuation the card uses, which
// covers every destination name a Latin-script trip produces (Rudesheim,
// Krakow, Istanbul, Malaga). Regenerate with:
//
//   curl -A 'Mozilla/4.0' 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;800'
//   curl -o w.ttf <the .ttf url that CSS names for each weight>
//   python3 -m fontTools.subset w.ttf --output-file=out.ttf --no-hinting \
//     --layout-features=kern,liga \
//     --unicodes='U+0020-00FF,U+0100-017F,U+2010-2015,U+2018-201D,U+2022,U+2026,U+00B7,U+20AC'
//   then base64 each file into the constants below.

export const OUTFIT_400 = '';

export const OUTFIT_800 = '';
